  "summary": "Moth wings, moss and meadow light: the internet moves into the fairy wood.",
  "description": "Fairycore is the woodland-fantasy branch of the pandemic-era nature aesthetics: dew-lit meadows, moth and butterfly wings, mushroom clusters, fairy-light glades, gossamer dresses and delicate jewelry — with fairygrunge adding dirt, twine and muted decay to the sweetness. It grew from Tumblr's cottagecore family via TikTok (2020-21 peak), feeding dress-up videos, nature-walk filming and wedding-inspo boards; cottagecore's domesticity becomes fairycore's wilderness. Its visual grammar: backlit fog, found-object altars, and the persistent sense that the camera wandered off the path and saw something it shouldn't have.",
  "culturalContext": "Fairycore was pandemic escapism's woodland form: TikTok's fairy costumes and moss-and-light filming defined 2020-21 nature dreaming, fed the cottagecore family's growth, and now shapes wedding styling and nature-content aesthetics as the internet's walk off the path.",
